{"schema_version":2,"entity_type":"bundle","questions":[],"pools":[],"exercises":[{"client_key":"recovery_comparatives_recover","title":"Comparatives — Recupera","description":"Ricostruisci forma, spelling, irregolari e than attraverso confronti chiari.","instructions":"Leggi il confronto prima di scegliere la forma.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A1+","topic":"comparatives","estimated_minutes":12,"settings":{"display_mode":"one_at_a_time","feedback_timing":"question_end","show_score":false,"show_correct_answers":true,"show_explanations":true,"show_diagnostic_summary":true,"allow_retry":true},"sections":[{"client_key":"recovery_comparatives_recover_section","title":"Recupera","instructions":"Leggi il confronto prima di scegliere la forma.","selection_mode":"fixed","feedback_timing":"question_end","questions":[{"client_key":"recovery_comparatives_recover_teaching","type":"content_block","title":"Comparatives: confronta due cose","prompt":"Prima di esercitarti","instructions":"Leggi le regole e osserva gli esempi.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A1+","topic":"comparatives","subtopic":"core","primary_skill":"grammar","learning_objective":"Compare two entities using the appropriate comparative form, spelling and than.","difficulty":"support","content":{"educational_schema_version":1,"template_id":"educational-content-block-v1","variant":"grammar","body":"Il comparativo serve a mettere due elementi a confronto. Prima riconosci il significato, poi scegli la forma.","intro":"Per un italofono i due errori più frequenti sono tradurre automaticamente con more e costruire forme doppie. In inglese devi scegliere una sola struttura comparativa.","sections":[{"key":"meaning","type":"rule","title":"Prima il confronto","body":"Usa il comparativo quando metti a confronto due persone, oggetti, luoghi o situazioni. La frase deve dire o rendere chiaro che una cosa ha una qualità in misura maggiore o minore dell'altra.","examples":[{"text":"The train is faster than the bus.","highlight":["faster than"]},{"text":"This exercise is easier.","highlight":["easier"]}]},{"key":"short","type":"pattern","title":"Aggettivi brevi: -er","body":"Con molti aggettivi brevi aggiungi -er. Se il secondo termine è espresso, usa than.","pattern":"short adjective + -er (+ than ...)","examples":[{"text":"cheap → cheaper","highlight":["cheaper"]},{"text":"small → smaller","highlight":["smaller"]},{"text":"The red bag is cheaper than the black one.","highlight":["cheaper than"]}]},{"key":"spelling","type":"rule","title":"Controlla lo spelling","body":"Con consonante + y, cambia y in i prima di -er. Con alcuni aggettivi brevi CVC raddoppia la consonante finale.","examples":[{"text":"easy → easier","highlight":["easier"]},{"text":"happy → happier","highlight":["happier"]},{"text":"big → bigger","highlight":["bigger"]}]},{"key":"long","type":"rule","title":"Aggettivi più lunghi: more","body":"Con molti aggettivi più lunghi usa more davanti all'aggettivo, senza aggiungere -er.","examples":[{"text":"comfortable → more comfortable","highlight":["more comfortable"]},{"text":"expensive → more expensive","highlight":["more expensive"]}]},{"key":"irregular","type":"comparison","title":"Good e bad cambiano forma","body":"Due comparativi molto frequenti sono irregolari: good → better e bad → worse.","correct":{"text":"This option is better, but it is more expensive.","highlight":["better","more expensive"]},"incorrect":{"text":"This option is more good.","highlight":["more good"]}},{"key":"double","type":"mistake","title":"Un solo comparativo","body":"Non usare more insieme a una forma già in -er.","correct":{"text":"This ticket is cheaper than that one.","highlight":["cheaper"]},"incorrect":{"text":"This ticket is more cheaper than that one.","highlight":["more cheaper"]}},{"key":"than","type":"mistake","title":"Than, non then","body":"Quando nomini il secondo termine del confronto, usa than. Then significa 'poi'.","correct":{"text":"My journey is shorter than yours.","highlight":["than"]},"incorrect":{"text":"My journey is shorter then yours.","highlight":["then"]}},{"key":"recap","type":"recap","title":"Prima di continuare","points":["Confronto tra due elementi.","Molti aggettivi brevi: -er.","Consonante + y: -ier; alcuni CVC raddoppiano.","Molti aggettivi lunghi: more + adjective.","good → better; bad → worse.","Secondo termine espresso: than."]}]},"grading":{"mode":"automatic","weight":0,"nearly_correct_multiplier":0.5},"feedback":{},"diagnostics":{"tested_codes":[],"fallback_error_code":null},"tags":["recovery","comparatives","recover","structured-teaching"],"foundation_links":[]},{"client_key":"recovery_comp_recover_1","type":"multiple_choice","title":"Due opzioni","prompt":"We have two routes. Route A is 4 km; Route B is 7 km. Route A is ___ Route B.","instructions":"Scegli la risposta corretta.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A1+","topic":"comparatives","subtopic":"short_adjectives","primary_skill":"grammar","learning_objective":"Choose a short-adjective comparative and than in a meaningful two-route comparison","difficulty":"support","content":{"options":[{"key":"a","text":"shorter than","is_correct":true},{"key":"b","text":"more short than","is_correct":false,"error_code":"COMPARATIVE_ER"},{"key":"c","text":"shorter then","is_correct":false,"error_code":"COMPARATIVE_THAN"}]},"grading":{"mode":"automatic","weight":1,"nearly_correct_multiplier":0.5},"feedback":{"explanation":"Short è breve: shorter. Per introdurre il secondo termine usa than."},"diagnostics":{"tested_codes":["COMPARATIVE_ER","COMPARATIVE_THAN"],"fallback_error_code":"COMPARATIVE_ER"},"tags":["recovery","comparatives"],"foundation_links":[]},{"client_key":"recovery_comp_recover_2","type":"select_gap","title":"Spelling nel confronto","prompt":"Completa le due frasi.","instructions":"Completa scegliendo la forma corretta.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A1+","topic":"comparatives","subtopic":"spelling","primary_skill":"grammar","learning_objective":"Apply y-to-ier and CVC doubling in common comparatives","difficulty":"support","content":{"text_template":"This homework is [[blank_1]] than yesterday's. My new bedroom is [[blank_2]] than the old one.","blanks":[{"key":"blank_1","accepted_answers":["easier"],"options":["easier","easyer","more easy"],"points":1,"feedback":{},"answer_error_mappings":[{"answer":"easyer","error_code":"COMPARATIVE_Y_IER"},{"answer":"more easy","error_code":"COMPARATIVE_ER"}]},{"key":"blank_2","accepted_answers":["bigger"],"options":["bigger","biger","more big"],"points":1,"feedback":{},"answer_error_mappings":[{"answer":"biger","error_code":"COMPARATIVE_DOUBLE_CONSONANT"},{"answer":"more big","error_code":"COMPARATIVE_ER"}]}]},"grading":{"mode":"per_blank","weight":1,"nearly_correct_multiplier":0.5},"feedback":{"explanation":"Easy → easier; big → bigger."},"diagnostics":{"tested_codes":["COMPARATIVE_Y_IER","COMPARATIVE_DOUBLE_CONSONANT"],"fallback_error_code":"COMPARATIVE_Y_IER"},"tags":["recovery","comparatives"],"foundation_links":[]},{"client_key":"recovery_comp_recover_3","type":"multiple_choice","title":"Una scelta più costosa","prompt":"The train costs €42 and the bus costs €18. The train is ___.","instructions":"Scegli la risposta corretta.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A1+","topic":"comparatives","subtopic":"long_adjectives","primary_skill":"grammar","learning_objective":"Use more with a common longer adjective","difficulty":"support","content":{"options":[{"key":"a","text":"more expensive","is_correct":true},{"key":"b","text":"expensiver","is_correct":false,"error_code":"COMPARATIVE_MORE"},{"key":"c","text":"more expensiver","is_correct":false,"error_code":"COMPARATIVE_MORE"}]},"grading":{"mode":"automatic","weight":1,"nearly_correct_multiplier":0.5},"feedback":{"explanation":"Expensive usa more: more expensive."},"diagnostics":{"tested_codes":["COMPARATIVE_MORE"],"fallback_error_code":"COMPARATIVE_MORE"},"tags":["recovery","comparatives"],"foundation_links":[]},{"c